@"A generic tuple of two values."
record Tuple<t1, t2> with val1(t1), val2(t2)

@"Group an array of objects by equivalance of a given key, returns the dictionary of groups."
action groupBy<t> on array(t[]), groupKey(literal) returns record Tuple<literal, t[]>[]

@"Find a dictionary value of the given key."
action findInDictionary<tk, tv> on dictionary(record Tuple<tk, tv>[]), key(tk) returns tv

@"A type spec reference. It only has a literal string *typeId*, which must be of `type-id := base-id ("[]")?`, and `base-id = "literal" | ("record" record-id generic-params) | type-id`. Here generic params are passed as `"<"t1,t2,...">"` if needed, and `t1,t2` are again type identifiers or generic names provided a generic context."
record TypeSpec with typeId(literal)

@"An add-record operation. It contains the complete RecordDef to be added to the ruleset."
record AddRecordDef with unit(record RecordDef)

@"An add-rule operation. It contains the complete RuleDef to be added to the ruleset."
record AddRuleDef with unit(record RuleDef)

@"An add-action operation. It contains the complete ActionDef to be added to the ruleset."
record AddAction with unit(record ActionDef)

@"A removal operation. It identifies a unit of a given type (among 'rule'|'record'|'action') to be removed by its unique id."
record RemoveRulesetUnit with type(literal), unitId(literal)

@"A replace-record operation. It provides the new full RecordDef whose id is the id of the target record to be replaced."
record ReplaceRecordDef with newUnit(record RecordDef)

@"A replace-rule operation. It provides the new full RuleDef whose id is the id of the target rule to be replaced."
record ReplaceRuleDef with newUnit(record RuleDef)

@"A replace-action operation. It provides the new full ActionDef whose id is the id of the target action to be replaced."
record ReplaceActionDef with newUnit(record ActionDef)

@"A compact description of a single ruleset unit, containing its unique id, its unit type (\"record\"|\"rule\"|\"action\"), and its natural language annotation."
record UnitSummary with
  id(literal), unitType(literal), annotation(literal)

@"A collection of ids (of records/rules/actions, respectively), which describes a query against the quleset requiring units of these ids."
record RulesetQuery with
  recordIds: literal[]
  ruleIds: literal[]
  actionIds: literal[]

@"Find units in the ruleset by semantic similarity to a literal query, return the similar units as an array of record UnitSummary."
action retrieveSimilarUnits on query(literal) returns record UnitSummary[]

@"Interprets a natural language type description phrase into a TypeSpec."
rule interpret-type-spec for typeDesc(literal)
given:
  availableUnits: result of retrieveSimilarUnits where query = $for.typeDesc
  groupedUnits: result of groupBy<record UnitSummary> where array = $given.availableUnits, groupKey = "unitType"
  availableRecords: result of findInDictionary<literal, record UnitSummary[]> where dictionary = $given.groupedUnits, key = "record"
  baseId: ref(literal) "the base type identifier that corresponds to the type described by '{$for.typeDesc}'. It must be one of 'literal', or a record id in {$given.availableRecords}, or a generic parameter name."
  arrayLayers: ref(literal) "the number of array layers for {$for.typeDesc}, for example, 0 for `literal`, \"an array of strings\" should be 1, and \"an array of string arrays\" is also allowed, having layer 2."
must be: ref(TypeSpec) "the fully assembled type id string, composed of {$given.baseId}, having {$given.arrayLayers} layers of array represented by appending that number of suffixes '[]'"

@"A rule definition. Contains an id, an annotation, its formal parameters (for-block), local bindings (given-block), and the final value expression (must-be)."
record RuleDef with
  id(literal), annotation(literal),
  forParams(record Tuple<literal, record TypeSpec>[]),
  givenBindings(record Tuple<literal, record ValueExpr>[]),  
  mustBe(record ValueExpr)

@"A value expression appearing in a rule, represented as a literal field whose value is a string in the ValueExpr DSL."
+"\nThe DSL is a line‑based format. Each line is one of:"
+"\n  - `var <name> [.<field> ...]`: variable reference with optional field path."
+"\n  - `"<template>"`: interpolated string."
+"\n  - `ref(<type>) "<subject>"`: sub‑interpretation. `<subject>` is a natural‑language noun phrase that describes the value the system is to construct; `<type>` is the expected type for the product."
+"\n  - `array [ <elem1>, <elem2>, ...]`: array literal."
+"\n  - `record <typeId> with <field1> = <expr>, <field2> = <expr>, ...`: record construction."
+"\n  - `satisfying <ruleId> where <arg1> = <expr>, ...`: definite rule call."
+"\n  - `result of <actionName> where <arg1> = <expr>, ...`: action call."
+"\n  - `seq <innerKind> <arg1> = (iter)? <expr>, ...`: sequential evaluation, where innerKind is `record...with`, `satisfying...where`, or `result of...where`, and `iter` is an optional keyword for expressions."
+"\nAll expressions that appear as arguments inside another expression are themselves represented as DSL strings."
record ValueExpr with dslText(literal)

@"Interprets a natural-language text that describes exactly one rule definition into a RuleDef."
+"\nIt must be declarative and interprative: it states what will be interpreted to what a standardized form, not the procedure to execute something."
+"\nIt should describe a subject to be interpreted, which may be parametrized among a whole subject type, then steps of intermediate interpretations/actions/record constructions. They should finally build to a standardized instance, which is \"what this subject will be interpreted to\"."
+"\nThe constraint can be put on the subject for the interpretation to run at better performance."
+"\nThe description shouldn't define new record shapes/actions inline. If also shouldn't just be a trivial extraction like output merely copies an input field; The interpretation must add structural/domain constraints, etc."
rule interpret-rule-def for rawText(literal)
given:
  ruleId: satisfying identify-def-subject where description = $for.rawText
  rawAnnotation:
    ref(literal) "the natural language annotation for this rule, describing the subject contract, taken from: {$for.rawText}"
  annotation: satisfying canonicalize-annotation where
    rawAnnot = $given.rawAnnotation, subjectType = "rule", subjectId = $given.ruleId, details = ""
  rawForParams:
    ref(record Tuple<literal, literal>[]) "the formal parameters of the rule as described in: {$for.rawText}. Each is a pair: parameter name and its natural language type description."
  forParamTypes: seq satisfying interpret-type-spec where typeDesc = iter $given.rawForParams.val2
  typedForParams: seq record Tuple<literal, record TypeSpec> with
    val1 = iter $given.rawForParams.val1,
    val2 = iter $given.forParamTypes
  rawGivenBindings:
    ref(record Tuple<literal, literal>[]) "the intermediate bindings described in: {$for.rawText}, where each binding has a name and a natural language expression description."
  givenBindingTypes: seq satisfying interpret-type-spec where typeDesc = iter $given.rawGivenBindings.val2
  givenBindings: seq record Tuple<literal, record ValueExpr> with
    val1 = iter $given.rawGivenBindings.val1,
    val2 = iter $given.givenBindingTypes
  mustBePhrase:
    ref(literal) "the natural language description of the final value expression (the 'must be' part) in: {$for.rawText}"
  mustBe: satisfying interpret-value-expr where phrase = $given.mustBePhrase
must be:
  record RuleDef with
    id = $given.ruleId,
    annotation = $given.annotation,
    forParams = $given.typedForParams,
    givenBindings = $given.givenBindings,
    mustBe = $given.mustBe

@"A record definition. It has a unique identifier *id*, an array *fields* of the full set of mandatory fields (a key-type typle for each), and an annotation that is the complete structural contract of the type (including any grammar syntax when applicable)."
record RecordDef with
  annotation(literal), id(literal), fields(record Tuple<literal, record TypeSpec>[])

@"Interprets a natural-language text that describes exactly one record type definition into a standardized RecordDef."
+"\nThe description must declare all mandatory fields with their names and a detailed type and structural description. And it should be purely structural and declarative: describing what shape the data has, not how it is computed or when it is used."
+"\nIt shouldn't contain any behavioural rules, any executable action definitions."
rule interpret-record-def for rawText(literal)
given:
  recordId: satisfying interpret-def-subject where description = $for.rawText
  rawAnnotation:
    ref(literal) "the natural language description that serves as the annotation for the record '{$given.recordId}', taken from: {$for.rawText}. It should describe the purpose and contract of this record type."
  fieldDescs: satisfying interpret-fields where recordDescription = $for.rawText
  fieldTypes: seq satisfying interpret-type-spec where typeDesc = iter $given.fieldDescs.val2
  constructedFields:
    seq record Tuple<literal, record TypeSpec> with
      val1 = iter $given.fieldDescs.val1,
      val2 = iter $given.fieldTypes
  detailsForAnnot:
    ref(literal) "a structured summary of the fields: {$given.constructedFields}"
  canonicalAnnotation: satisfying canonicalize-annotation where
    rawAnnot = $given.rawAnnotation, subjectType = "record",
    subjectId = $given.recordId, details = $given.detailsForAnnot
must be:
  record RecordDef with
    id = $given.recordId,
    fields = $given.constructedFields,
    annotation = $given.canonicalAnnotation

@"An action definition. Contains the action's name, annotation, formal parameters, output type, and an actual Lua script implementation of the action."
record ActionDef with
  name(literal), annotation(literal),
  params(record Tuple<literal, record TypeSpec>[]),
  outputType(record TypeSpec),
  luaScript(literal)

@"Interprets a natural-language text that describes exactly one action definition into an ActionDef."
+"\nThe description must describe an \"action\", which is to be applied to a set of typed parameters."
+"\nThen describe a domain-indepentent, atomic operation on these params which does not contain any semantic logic, any rule/action call, and isn't a simple action composable from field accessing/record construction. This needs to produce a final result."
+"\nIt shouldn't describe a record shape or a behavioural rule, nor do rule‑specific interpretations."
rule interpret-action-def for rawText(literal)
given:
  actionName: satisfying identify-def-subject where description = $for.rawText
  rawAnnotation: ref(literal) "the natural language annotation for the action, taken from: {$for.rawText}"
  annotation: satisfying canonicalize-annotation where
    rawAnnot = $given.rawAnnotation, subjectType = "action", subjectId = $given.actionName, details = ""
  rawParams:
    ref(record Tuple<literal, literal>[]) "the formal parameters described in: {$for.rawText}"
  paramTypes: seq satisfying interpret-type-spec where typeDesc = iter $given.rawParams.val2
  typedParams: seq record Tuple<literal, record TypeSpec> with
    val1 = iter $given.rawParams.val1,
    val2 = iter $given.paramTypes
  outputTypeDesc:
    ref(literal) "the natural language description of the output type, as stated in: {$for.rawText}"
  outputType: satisfying interpret-type-spec where typeDesc = $given.outputTypeDesc
  operationDesc:
    ref(literal) "the pure, domain-independent operation description extracted from: {$for.rawText}. This description should state what the action does without referencing business logic."
  luaScript:
    ref(literal) "a Lua script that implements an action with name '{$given.actionName}', parameters {$given.typedParams}, output type {$given.outputType}, and operation: '{$given.operationDesc}'"
must be:
  record ActionDef with
    name = $given.actionName,
    annotation = $given.annotation,
    params = $given.typedParams,
    outputType = $given.outputType,
    luaScript = $given.luaScript

@"Describe a section in the ruleset, containing the full definitions or records/rules/actions, respectively."
record RulesetSection with
  records: RecordDef[]
  rules: RuleDef[]
  actions: ActionDef[]

@"From a RulesetQuery which describes the desired ids, find the corresponding RulesetSection matching these query ids."
action findSectionInRuleset on query(record RulesetQuery) returns record RulesetSection

@"Interprets a natural‑language phrase that describes an expectation about desired units in the ruleset."
+"\nIt returns an array of UnitSummary entries for the ruleset units that are semantically relevant to that expectation."
rule interpret-relevant-units for expectationPhrase(literal)
given:
  rawSummaries: result of retrieveSimilarUnits where query = $for.expectationPhrase
  groupedSummaries: result of groupBy<record UnitSummary> where array = $given.rawSummaries, groupKey = "unitType"
  recordSummaries: result of findInDictionary<literal, record UnitSummary[]> where dictionary = $given.groupedSummaries, key = "record"
  ruleSummaries: result of findInDictionary<literal, record UnitSummary[]> where dictionary = $given.groupedSummaries, key = "rule"
  actionsSummaries: result of findInDictionary<literal, record UnitSummary[]> where dictionary = $given.groupedSummaries, key = "action"
  rulesetQuery: ref(record RulesetQuery) "the ids of ruleset units within records: {$given.recordSummaries}, rules: {$given.ruleSummaries}, actions: {$given.actionSummaries}, which need their details queried to meet the expectation: {$for.expectationPhrase}"
must be: result of findSectionInRuleset where query = $given.rulesetQuery

@"Interprets a literal project items expectation into a literal expectation of a ruleset item."
rule interpret-project-items for expectationPhrase(literal)
must be:
  rulesetExp = ref(literal) "an expectation literal of existing ruleset items which fully describe the expectation for project items: {$for.expectationPhrase}"
